- pod1230objectives.177.desc: "The Azure Dragon Court was instituted as the ruling Court for Japan and Korea when the Orthodox (and Chinese aligned) [Glossary('Dharma','podgloss.dharma')] spread to the islands long ago. Since then, Japan has grown in influence, sometimes even being the center of the court themselves. This has caused frictions with the mainland that still sees Japan as a somewhat unruly "little brother" in need of guidance.\nWith the slow decline of the mainland Courts and the consolidation of Japan's power, it was just a matter of time before the split was made official. It has been done tonight and the outraged Chinese and Korean $pod_kueijin$ can do little but curse and spout empty threats of retaliation.\nThe Azure Dragon Court is no more and the Uji Courts now stand as a new contender in the nightly political landscape of East Asia.\n\nAs the ruler who formally announced this split, you have to handle the aftermath and the many minor vampires of Chinese or Korean allegiance that remains in Japan.\nSome clans advice for a peaceful parting, letting them stay or leave as they please as long as they follow the new rules. Other, more aggressive, clans argue for an harsher retribution, seizing their assets and kicking them out of the islands by force."
