- pod1230objectives.200.desc: "The Black Tortoise Court has always been something of an outsider among the August Courts. Considered strange, or complicit to hostile foreigners because of its ties to the steppes, it has always earned only tense respect at best or outright hostility at worst from its peers.\nWhen the [Glossary('Anda','podgloss.anda')] started pushing from the west and the $pod_akuma$ caused troubles internally, other Courts weren't really shedding tears, the Yellow Emperor Court going as far as to attack it at its weakest.\nWith its indolent leadership unable to react to these issues, the fall of the Black Tortoise Court seemed like a foregone conclusion. But it seems that the Heavens still have a place for the Demons of Xia. A focused effort has recently seen the once beleaguered Court triumphing over many of its neighbors and restoring its hegemony over the steppes.\n\nThe Black Tortoise Court didn't forget the past however. Old feuds never truly die for the immortals and the Court has now begun a renewed campaign of aggression, perhaps inspired by their steppe roots, claiming even most of Northern China in the process."
