+ nick_suwarian_father: "Father of Suwarian"
  podgreatpersons.0210.t: "Al-Hajj Salim Suwari"
- podgreatpersons.0210.desc: "Hailing from the Sahelian town of Ja in the core Mali area, Al-Hajj Salim Suwari has performed the pilgrimage (hajj) to Mecca several times and devoted his intellectual career to developing an understanding of the faith that would assist Muslim minorities in residing in "pagan" lands.\nHe formulated an important theological rationale for peaceful coexistence with the non-Muslim ruling classes called the Suwarian tradition.\nAs the tension between native Laibon and [Glossary('Ashirra','game_concept_ashirra_desc')] vampires traveling with the Muslim traders grow, having a man who has devoted his considerable intellect to making bridges between the two communities could be of help."
+ podgreatpersons.0210.desc: "Hailing from the Sahelian town of Ja in the core Mali area, Al-Hajj Salim Suwari has performed the pilgrimage (hajj) to Mecca several times and devoted his intellectual career to developing an understanding of the faith that would assist Muslim minorities in residing in \"pagan\" lands.\nHe formulated an important theological rationale for peaceful coexistence with the non-Muslim ruling classes called the Suwarian tradition.\nAs the tension between native Laibon and [Glossary('Ashirra','game_concept_ashirra_desc')] vampires traveling with the Muslim traders grows, having a man who has devoted his considerable intellect to making bridges between the two communities could be of help."
  nick_the_resurrected: "the Resurrected"       
  podgreatpersons.0211.t: "Kristos Samra"
- podgreatpersons.0211.desc: "A strange story has come to your attention lately.\nKristos Samra was born into a wealthy and pious family from a frontier province in the Christian Ethiopian empire. When she was around forty years old, one day she became enraged with a badly behaved maidservant and thrust a firebrand down her throat and the maidservant died. Then Kristos Samra felt terrible and guilty and prayed for God to restore the life of the maidservant. Fortunately her prayer was answered and the maid was alive again. So Kristos Samra was amazed and she felt "if God hears my prayer while I'm in this worldly life how much will he answer my prayer in monastery?". She decided to be a nun and has since started her journey to a spiritual life.\nWhile her faith puts her out of your reach, you are intrigued by the prospect of (apparently) a simple mortal performing a resurrection. As a nun, Kristos Samra has no use for her miraculously saved maidservant anymore, which would make it easy for you to study this mysterious returned from death woman yourself."
+ podgreatpersons.0211.desc: "A strange story has come to your attention lately.\nKristos Samra was born into a wealthy and pious family from a frontier province in the Christian Ethiopian empire. When she was around forty years old, one day she became enraged with a badly behaved maidservant and thrust a firebrand down her throat and the maidservant died. Then Kristos Samra felt terrible and guilty and prayed for God to restore the life of the maidservant. Fortunately her prayer was answered and the maid was alive again. So Kristos Samra was amazed and she felt \"if God hears my prayer while I'm in this worldly life, how much will he answer my prayers in a monastery?\". She decided to be a nun and has since started her journey to a spiritual life.\nWhile her faith puts her out of your reach, you are intrigued by the prospect of (apparently) a simple mortal performing a resurrection. As a nun, Kristos Samra has no use for her miraculously saved maidservant anymore, which would make it easy for you to study this mysterious resurrected woman yourself."
  Ugolino_Vivaldi: "Ugolino Vivaldi"            
  nick_the_first_explorer: "the First Explorer"            
  podgreatpersons.0212.t: "Ugolino Vivaldi"
  podgreatpersons.0212.desc: "A strange embarkation washed ashore not too far away from your domain recently. Apparently struck by a storm, most of the unfortunate crew didn't survive their brutal arrival on your land. One however escaped this ordeal wounded but alive.\nIt took some time to understand his language but it seems he is named Ugolino Vivaldi and comes from a city named Genoa. He and his brother (who didn't survive) were chartering an expedition to India.\nStranded, alone in a foreign land and with no knowledge of the area, this man is basically at your mercy. He certainly has an adventurous spirit and a good head for numbers (apparently being a merchant as well as a captain) which could both prove useful to your cause."
  Kassi: "Kassi"
  nick_qasa: "Qasa"
- podgreatpersons.0213.desc: "Principal wife of the Malian Emperor Suleyman, Kassi ruled jointly with her husband. She was extremely popular with the royal court, which counted many of her relations among its members. But she soon fell out of favor with her husband, who preferred a commoner named Bendjou. Eventually, he divorced her to marry the latter. The noble ladies of the court took Kassi's side, continuing to recognize her legitimacy and refusing to honor the new royal wife. Such insubordination – they threw earth on their heads to honor Kassi while throwing earth on their hands to insult Bendjou – soon angered Suleyman and his new wife, to the point that Kassi was forced to seek sanctuary in the mosque.\nCivil war soon erupted, as she encouraged the nobility, including her relations, to revolt. The war was a struggle between two ideological factions; one group supported Suleyman, while the other supported not only Kassi but sons of the former ruler, Maghan. Suleyman and his chiefs eventually defeated Kassi and her cousins, discrediting her by showing that she and her cousin, Djathal, who had been banished for treason, were in league together.\nThis recent defeat has offered you an opportunity. You could "rescue" Kassi before Suleyman's men close in on her. She has certainly proved a keen mind for politics despite her defeat."
+ podgreatpersons.0213.desc: "Principal wife of the Malian Emperor Suleyman, Kassi ruled jointly with her husband. She was extremely popular with the royal court, which counted many of her relations among its members. But she soon fell out of favor with her husband, who preferred a commoner named Bendjou. Eventually, he divorced her to marry the latter. The noble ladies of the court took Kassi's side, continuing to recognize her legitimacy and refusing to honor the new royal wife. Such insubordination – they threw earth on their heads to honor Kassi while throwing earth on their hands to insult Bendjou – soon angered Suleyman and his new wife, to the point that Kassi was forced to seek sanctuary in the mosque.\nCivil war soon erupted, as she encouraged the nobility, including her relations, to revolt. The war was a struggle between two ideological factions; one group supported Suleyman, while the other supported not only Kassi but sons of the former ruler, Maghan. Suleyman and his chiefs eventually defeated Kassi and her cousins, discrediting her by showing that she and her cousin, Djathal, who had been banished for treason, were in league together.\nThis recent defeat has offered you an opportunity. You could \"rescue\" Kassi before Suleyman's men close in on her. She has certainly proved a keen mind for politics despite her defeat."
  nick_the_cuman: "the Cuman"         
  podgreatpersons.0214.t: "Elizabeth the Cuman"
- podgreatpersons.0214.desc: "When her father, Khan Koten of the Cumans, negotiated peace with the Hungarians after a lengthy war, Elizabeth was wed to the then Prince Stephen. Upon her wedding, Elizabeth converted to Roman Catholicism although many at court were doubtful of her real devotion to her new religion. Her tenure as Queen was unremarkable but she was soon propelled to the front seat when her husband died and she became Queen Regent for her son Ladislaus.\nThe young boy soon showed a deep appreciation for his mother's Cuman heritage and encouraged political moves to favor them, which the court attributed to Elizabeth's "pagan" influence. As such, Elizabeth's regency, and Ladislaus's reign, were full of civil wars and palace coups. The latest in this succession has seen Ladislaus perish, leaving little doubt as to Elizabeth's ultimate fate now that the hostile court has regained control. It might be time for you to intervene if you see the experienced Queen as a potential $pod_ghoul$ or $pod_Embrace$ candidate."
+ podgreatpersons.0214.desc: "When her father, Khan Koten of the Cumans, negotiated peace with the Hungarians after a lengthy war, Elizabeth was wed to the then Prince Stephen. Upon her wedding, Elizabeth converted to Roman Catholicism although many at court were doubtful of her real devotion to her new religion. Her tenure as Queen was unremarkable but she was soon propelled to the front seat when her husband died and she became Queen Regent for her son Ladislaus.\nThe young boy soon showed a deep appreciation for his mother's Cuman heritage and encouraged political moves to favor them, which the court attributed to Elizabeth's \"pagan\" influence. As such, Elizabeth's regency, and Ladislaus's reign, were full of civil wars and palace coups. The latest in this succession has seen Ladislaus perish, leaving little doubt as to Elizabeth's ultimate fate now that the hostile court has regained control. It might be time for you to intervene if you see the experienced Queen as a potential $pod_ghoul$ or $pod_Embrace$ candidate."
  syrgiannes_palaiologos: "Syrgiannes Palaiologos"  
  nick_the_shifting: "the Shifting"            
- podgreatpersons.0215.desc: "You have recently learned that the career of one of the most infamous man of the Byzantine Empire is soon coming to an end. Syrgiannes Palaiologos's life is almost a lesson in treachery and unbridled ambition. He betrayed two emperors, multiple childhood friends, broke several treaties and seduced the Byzantine Empress in his constant bids for power and gold. Arrested several times, he always managed to somehow get on the good side of his captors... before betraying them once again when the time was right.\nSyrgiannes Palaiologos is also an adequate military commander (his official post despite his constant politicking) and has experience with governing regions, skills that would make him valuable to a $pod_cainite$ lord bold enough to not fear his deceitful nature.\nHe is currently working for the Serbs, leading an invasion of Byzantium for them, but his luck has finally ran out as you have learned that the peace talks offered by the Emperor are just a facade for an opportunity to kill Syrgiannes once and for all. A good time to act if that is your wish."
- podgreatpersons.0216.desc: "Through the excited murmurs of mortals under your rule, you learned of an upcoming duel between two legendary warriors and bitter rivals: Sasaki Kojirō and Miyamoto Musashi. Kojirō seems to be the favored one among the people thanks to his undeniable elegance and charisma. A student of the legendary Toda Seigen, he serves a respected daimyo as hatamoto and sword instructor. Kojirō is renowned for his mastery of the lightning-quick and regal Ganryū style which earned him the moniker "Demon of the Western Provinces". Sasaki is a master swordsman, yet you have a feeling that his honorable way of fighting may not earn him victory over his more pragmatic rival. An official of the Hosokawa Clan witnessing the legitimacy of the duel, maybe convinced to remove a wounded Kojirō from the scene quickly, right into your hands."           
+ podgreatpersons.0215.desc: "You have recently learned that the career of one of the most infamous men of the Byzantine Empire is soon coming to an end. Syrgiannes Palaiologos's life is almost a lesson in treachery and unbridled ambition. He betrayed two emperors, multiple childhood friends, broke several treaties and seduced the Byzantine Empress in his constant bids for power and gold. Arrested several times, he always managed to somehow get on the good side of his captors... before betraying them once again when the time was right.\nSyrgiannes Palaiologos is also an adequate military commander (his official post despite his constant politicking) and has experience with governing regions, skills that would make him valuable to a $pod_cainite$ lord bold enough to not fear his deceitful nature.\nHe is currently working for the Serbs, leading an invasion of Byzantium for them, but his luck has finally run out as you have learned that the peace talks offered by the Emperor are just a facade for an opportunity to kill Syrgiannes once and for all. A good time to act if that is your wish."
  podgreatpersons.0216.t: "Sasaki Kojiro"
+ podgreatpersons.0216.desc: "Through the excited murmurs of mortals under your rule, you learned of an upcoming duel between two legendary warriors and bitter rivals: Sasaki Kojirō and Miyamoto Musashi. Kojirō seems to be the favored one among the people thanks to his undeniable elegance and charisma. A student of the legendary Toda Seigen, he serves a respected daimyo as hatamoto and sword instructor. Kojirō is renowned for his mastery of the lightning-quick and regal Ganryū style which earned him the moniker \"Demon of the Western Provinces\". Sasaki is a master swordsman, yet you have a feeling that his honorable way of fighting may not earn him victory over his more pragmatic rival. An official of the Hosokawa Clan witnessing the legitimacy of the duel could maybe be convinced to remove a wounded Kojirō from the scene quickly, right into your hands."
  podgreatpersons.0217.t: "Hwang Jini"
- podgreatpersons.0217.desc: "Born out of wedlock, Hwang Jini was considered untouchable, despite her remarkable beauty and wits. To escape that fate, she chose the path of the [Glossary('kisaeng','podgloss.kisaeng')|l], becoming a courtesan, poet and master of the gayageum, known under the name of Myeongwol.\nHer legendary beauty and astute mind made her well known and desired by many, even if her standing would not allow anyone to marry her. From all over Joseon, men came to her, trying to solve the Jeomiligu Idubulchool, a riddle that anyone who wanted to be her lover had to solve first. She also wrote some of the best sijo, her most famous one, "Blue Stream" is about her longing for a lover, and the struggling she felt performing as a kisaeng.\nShe's now retiring from her obligation, focusing on writing poetry, isolating herself from her social circle and maybe you could try to solve the Jeomiligu Idubulchool one last time."
+ podgreatpersons.0217.desc: "Born out of wedlock, Hwang Jini was considered untouchable, despite her remarkable beauty and wits. To escape that fate, she chose the path of the [Glossary('kisaeng','podgloss.kisaeng')|l], becoming a courtesan, poet and master of the gayageum, known under the name of Myeongwol.\nHer legendary beauty and astute mind made her well known and desired by many, even if her standing would not allow anyone to marry her. From all over Joseon, men came to her, trying to solve the Jeomiligu Idubulchool, a riddle that anyone who wanted to be her lover had to solve first. She also wrote some of the best sijo, her most famous one, \"Blue Stream\" is about her longing for a lover, and the struggles she felt performing as a kisaeng.\nShe's now retiring from her obligations, focusing on writing poetry, isolating herself from her social circle and maybe you could try to solve the Jeomiligu Idubulchool one last time."
  podgreatpersons.0218.t: "Yang Miaozhen"
- podgreatpersons.0218.desc: "In her youth, Yang Miaozhen was the wife and battlefield equal of Li Quan, the bandit leader of the legendary Red Coat Army of Shandong. After Li Quan's death, Yang Miaozhen took over the Red Coats herself, leading it to further victories that forced the Mongols to appoint her imperial governor of Shandong. It's been decades since then. Yang Miaozhen now enjoys a quiet rural retirement with her adopted son as successor. Nobody would question her disappearance, if a convincing corpse could be found..."                            
- podgreatpersons.0219.desc: "From the moment he took up arms, Kusunoki Masasue became a figure of unwavering loyalty and tactical brilliance. A devoted supporter of Emperor Go-Daigo, he led daring guerrilla campaigns against the Ashikaga forces along with his older brother Masashige, using strategy and deception to achieve near-impossible victories. While his brother is more renowned, Masasue himself is no less impressive on his own and he would likely be a loyal servant, if you so wished. Though the brothers have now been ordered to meet a superior foe by Emperor Go-Daigo, you still have a small window of time to intervene and take the loyal Little Dragon into your service."
+ podgreatpersons.0218.desc: "In her youth, Yang Miaozhen was the wife and battlefield equal of Li Quan, the bandit leader of the legendary Red Coat Army of Shandong. After Li Quan's death, Yang Miaozhen took over the Red Coats herself, leading it to further victories that forced the Mongols to appoint her imperial governor of Shandong. It's been decades since then. Yang Miaozhen now enjoys a quiet rural retirement with her adopted son as successor. Nobody would question her disappearance, if a convincing corpse could be found..."
