+ podgreatpersons.0224.t: "Yu Zijun"
  podgreatpersons.0224.desc: "The Chinese governor of the Ordos loop, Yu Zijun, has served ably and honestly. In fact, his signature proposal, to build a series of earthwork walls across the northern frontier, was key to ambushing and routing a large Mongol invasion. Yet, as of late, he's become the victim of court intrigue and stripped of his ranks. It might be worth recruiting a man of his competence."
- podgreatpersons.0224.t: "Yu Zijun"     
- podgreatpersons.0225.desc: "For all their wealth and patronage, the emperors of the Song Dynasty needed many #EMP daibi#!, or female ghostwriters to perform the writing and calligraphy that their rulers could not. One #EMP daibi #! was even talented enough to become the official consort of Emperor Duzong, despite her lack of beauty and pedigree. She earned the name Zhaoyi, or 'Luminous Deportment.'\n\nIt's been years since the Song court fell, but those who worked for it still recognize a certain talented poet of the Yuan court. She bears a different name now, and has written little of anything. Yet rumors swirl of a beautiful song she carved onto a tavern wall while taken north. Perhaps she still has a few verses left in her, for a more discerning ear."
- podgreatpersons.0225.t: "Wang Qinghui"   
+ podgreatpersons.0225.t: "Wang Qinghui"
+ podgreatpersons.0225.desc: "For all their wealth and patronage, the emperors of the Song Dynasty needed many #EMP daibi#!, or female ghostwriters, to perform the writing and calligraphy that their rulers could not. One #EMP daibi#! was even talented enough to become the official consort of Emperor Duzong, despite her lack of beauty and pedigree. She earned the name Zhaoyi, or 'Luminous Deportment'.\n\nIt's been years since the Song court fell, but those who worked for it still recognize a certain talented poet of the Yuan court. She bears a different name now, and has written little of anything. Yet rumors swirl of a beautiful song she carved onto a tavern wall while taken north. Perhaps she still has a few verses left in her, for a more discerning ear."
  podgreatpersons.0226.t: "Chǒng Tojǒn"
- podgreatpersons.0226.desc: "Taejo of Joseon is the face and muscle of the reform of Korea, replacing the crumbling Goryo dynasty. But the brain behind this reform, the philosopher that chose Confucianism over Buddhism, the administrator who codified most of the ambitious reform in the [Glossary('Joseon Gyeonggukjeon','podgloss.joseon_gyeonggukjeon')] is Chǒng Tojǒn.\nTrying to secure the eighth son of Taejo position to the throne, Chǒng Tojǒn participated in a palace plot to kill the fifth son of Taejo, starting the First Strife of Prince. Horrified by what his sons were willing to do to each other, Taejo abdicated in favor of his second son after only six years of reign.\nChǒng Tojǒn will pay the price of his support soon, and rumor has it that he already started writing a death poem. If you want to save this brilliant mind, now is the time to act."
+ podgreatpersons.0226.desc: "Taejo of Joseon is the face and muscle of the reformation of Korea, replacing the crumbling Goryeo dynasty. But the brain behind this reform, the philosopher that chose Confucianism over Buddhism, the administrator who codified most of the ambitious reforms in the [Glossary('Joseon Gyeonggukjeon','podgloss.joseon_gyeonggukjeon')] is Chǒng Tojǒn.\nTrying to secure the eighth son of Taejo's position to the throne, Chǒng Tojǒn participated in a palace plot to kill the fifth son of Taejo, starting the First Strife of Princes. Horrified by what his sons were willing to do to each other, Taejo abdicated in favor of his second son after only six years of reign.\nChǒng Tojǒn will pay the price of his support soon, and rumor has it that he already started writing a death poem. If you want to save this brilliant mind, now is the time to act."
  podgreatpersons.0227.t: "Ju Nongae"
- podgreatpersons.0227.desc: "You've been keeping an eye on Ju Nongae, a [Glossary('kisaeng','podgloss.kisaeng')|l], since your retainers told you about her beauty and how she managed to secure herself a position as the mistress of Choi Geyong-hwi, a local magistrate who was in charge of prosecuting her mother. When the Japanese started the Imjin war, Nongae stood by the side of her lover and master when he tried to organise the province defense, before being eventually defeated and killed.\nThe Japanese occupants forced all #EMP kisaeng #! to serve them at the Choseokru Pavillon. Deciding to avenge the death of Choi Gewong-hwi, Ju Nongae used her beauty to lure Keyamura Rokusuke, the Japanese general, to join her on a cliff over the Nam river, where she embraced him, lock her hand around his neck and threw both of them down the cliff into the river to an inevitable death.\nYour retainer found her on the river bank, barely breathing, her beauty fleeting as she's going through her last breathe. If you had plans for her, you must act now and decide if you want to $pod_Embrace$ her or not."
+ podgreatpersons.0227.desc: "You've been keeping an eye on Ju Nongae, a [Glossary('kisaeng','podgloss.kisaeng')|l], since your retainers told you about her beauty and how she managed to secure herself a position as the mistress of Choi Geyong-hwi, a local magistrate who was in charge of prosecuting her mother. When the Japanese started the Imjin war, Nongae stood by the side of her lover and master when he tried to organise the province's defenses, before being eventually defeated and killed.\nThe Japanese occupants forced all #EMP kisaeng#! to serve them at the Choseokru Pavillon. Deciding to avenge the death of Choi Gewong-hwi, Ju Nongae used her beauty to lure Keyamura Rokusuke, the Japanese general, to join her on a cliff over the Nam river, where she embraced him, locked her hand around his neck and threw both of them down the cliff to an inevitable death.\nYour retainer found her on the river bank, barely breathing, her beauty fleeting as she's going through her last breaths. If you had plans for her, you must act now and decide if you want to $pod_Embrace$ her or not."
  podgreatpersons.0228.t: "Dae Jang-geum"
- podgreatpersons.0228.desc: "Coming from humble beginnings and becoming a [Glossary('ǔinyǒ','podgloss.uinyo')|l], Jang-geum worked hard to secure the trust of King Jungjong. Even if she failed to save Queen Janggyeong while she was giving birth to the heir to the throne, Jungjong asked her to become his personal physician.\nHer approach to curing ailments through food proved both ground breaking and efficient, and cured numerous sickness striking the king. He finally died a peaceful death of old age, freeing Dae Jang-geum from her service.\nShe retired, taking up on her to train other #italic ǔinyǒ#! but her health seems to finally be giving up.\nNow is the time to go and meet her if you are curious to figure out what the Dae could do with the gift of the $pod_Embrace$." 
- podgreatpersons.0230.desc: "Buddhist monks are a common sight, but the presence of a controversial sage has garnered your attention. An old monk named Shinran, founder of the True Pure Land Buddhism has apparently been challenging traditional monastic beliefs for a long time now. He was exiled due to the stunning growth and popularity of his teachings, and during this exile Shinran married, openly challenging the monastic celibacy beliefs. His teachings seem to emphasize reliance on Amida’s Vow for salvation and faith in Buddha’s grace over anything else. An exiled learned man may be useful to have in your court, if you wish."          
- podgreatpersons.0230.t: "Shinran"  
+ podgreatpersons.0228.desc: "Coming from humble beginnings and becoming a [Glossary('ǔinyǒ','podgloss.uinyo')|l], Jang-geum worked hard to secure the trust of King Jungjong. Even if she failed to save Queen Janggyeong while she was giving birth to the heir to the throne, Jungjong asked her to become his personal physician.\nHer approach to curing ailments through food proved both groundbreaking and efficient, and cured numerous sicknesses striking the king. He finally died a peaceful death of old age, freeing Dae Jang-geum from her service.\nShe retired, taking up the task of training other #italic ǔinyǒ#!, but her health seems to finally be giving up.\nNow is the time to go and meet her if you are curious to figure out what the Dae could do with the gift of the $pod_Embrace$."
+ podgreatpersons.0230.t: "Shinran"
+ podgreatpersons.0230.desc: "Buddhist monks are a common sight, but the presence of a controversial sage has garnered your attention. An old monk named Shinran, founder of the True Pure Land Buddhist school, has apparently been challenging traditional monastic beliefs for a long time now. He was exiled due to the stunning growth and popularity of his teachings, and during this exile Shinran married, openly challenging the monastic tradition of celibacy. His teachings seem to emphasize reliance on Amida’s Vow for salvation and faith in Buddha’s grace over anything else. An exiled learned man may be useful to have in your court, if you wish."
  podgreatpersons.0231.t: "Kim T'ong-jǒng"
- podgreatpersons.0231.desc: "When King Wonjong surrendered to Kubilai Khan's demand and dismantled the military government of Goryeo, the [Glossary('sambyeolcho','podgloss.sambyeolcho')] refused the order and started a rebellion.\nOutnumbered they lead a campaign of guerilla from Jindo Island, harassing harbors, destroying the Yuan's and Goryeo's fleet and gathering intelligence. Eventually, the guerilla fell and fled to the small island of Tamna under the leadership of Kim T'ong-jǒng, the last of the #italic sambyeolcho#!.\nIf you want to give that fierce leader a chance to take on his revenge against the mongol, you should go to Tamna now and secure him, before the joint armies of Kubilai Khan and Wongjong destroy what's left of the rebelion."
+ podgreatpersons.0231.desc: "When King Wonjong surrendered to Kubilai Khan's demands and dismantled the military government of Goryeo, the [Glossary('sambyeolcho','podgloss.sambyeolcho')] refused the order and started a rebellion.\nOutnumbered, they led a campaign of guerilla warfare from Jindo Island, harassing harbors, destroying the Yuan's and Goryeo's fleet and gathering intelligence. Eventually, the guerilla fell and fled to the small island of Tamna under the leadership of Kim T'ong-jǒng, the last of the #italic sambyeolcho#!.\nIf you want to give that fierce leader a chance to take his revenge against the Mongols, you should go to Tamna now and secure him, before the joint armies of Kubilai Khan and Wongjong destroy what's left of the rebellion."
  podgreatpersons.0232.t: "Borjigin Yilianzhenbala"
- podgreatpersons.0232.desc: "To maintain a hold on the Goryeo, the Yuan dynasty send their daughters to marry the Goryeo's king. Yilianzhenbala has been married with King Chungsuk for three years, but the infatuation of the King with the Virtuous Consort Hong, one of his Goryeo wife, women has taken a toll on her sanity, to the point she openly confronted her husband during a banquet. The two of them fought and, since that day, she's been having frequent unexpliqued nose bleeds.\nYour retainers has been contacted by one of her servant, asking them if you could help her master to get out of reach of the King and enact vengeance on her rival. You're wondering how much Yilianzhenbala knows of your actual nature but her character and determination makes her an interesting $pod_Embrace$ prospect."
+ podgreatpersons.0232.desc: "To maintain a hold on the Goryeo, the Yuan dynasty send their daughters to marry the Goryeo's king. Yilianzhenbala has been married with King Chungsuk for three years, but the infatuation of the King with the Virtuous Consort Hong, one of his Goryeo wives, has taken a toll on her sanity, to the point she openly confronted her husband during a banquet. The two of them fought and, since that day, she's been having frequent unexpliqued nose bleeds.\nYour retainers have been contacted by one of her servants, asking if you could help her master get out of reach of the King and enact vengeance on her rival. You're wondering how much Yilianzhenbala knows of your actual nature but her character and determination make her an interesting $pod_Embrace$ prospect."
  podgreatpersons.0233.t: "Ulus Bukha"
- podgreatpersons.0233.desc: "Military commander and administrator for the Yuan dynasty in Ssangseong, Ulus Bhuka he migrated back to Hamju when the Goryeo started to reclaim their lands against the Mongols. He met Ch'oe Uihye on a business travel to her father's house, and immediately fell in love with her direct and sensual ways. Ulus Bhuka then adopted the name Yi Chach'un and defected to Goryeo.\nOf their two children, Yi Sõng Ye is following his father career but his ambitions are for the whole of Goryeo, planning a reform to resist the crumbling Yuan dominion, adopting neo-confucianism as the core tenets of what he calls the Joseon.\nBut Yi Chach'un will not live long enough to see his son becoming [Glossary('Taejo of Joseon','podgloss.taejo_joseon')]. He finds himself surrournded by a Red Turban raid and there's not a lot of time for you to move and seize the father of the future leader of Goryeo."
+ podgreatpersons.0233.desc: "A military commander and administrator for the Yuan dynasty in Ssangseong, Ulus Bhuka migrated back to Hamju when the Goryeo started to reclaim their lands against the Mongols. He met Ch'oe Uihye on a business trip to her father's house, and immediately fell in love with her direct and sensual ways. Ulus Bhuka then adopted the name Yi Chach'un and defected to Goryeo.\nOf their two children, Yi Sõng Ye is following his father's career but his ambitions are for the whole of Goryeo, planning a reform to resist the crumbling Yuan dominion, adopting neo-confucianism as the core tenets of what he calls the Joseon.\nBut Yi Chach'un will not live long enough to see his son becoming [Glossary('Taejo of Joseon','podgloss.taejo_joseon')]. He finds himself surrournded by a Red Turban raid and there's not a lot of time for you to move and seize the father of the future leader of Goryeo."
  podgreatpersons.0234.t: "Choe Yong-deok"
- podgreatpersons.0234.desc: "Yong-deok is born a [Glossary('nobi','podgloss.nobi')|l] and worked as a palace lady before catching the eye of King U, of the Goryeo. Quickly becoming a Royal Consort, she played the few cards she had well to maintain influence on King U, despite his interests in others #italic nobi#!.\nWhile U was trying to use the rise of the Ming to remove Goryeo from the Chinese dominion, Yong-deok lost his favor, was accused of plotting and was banished from court. Her family was executed and their body publicly displayed.\nBut the King fickle mind and ambition, leading him to push against the Ming despite his advisor council, will quickly change his mind regarding Yong-deok and he will reinstate and pardon her.\nKing U will fall evengually, and Yong-deok will be removed from the court, going back to be a #italic nobi#!, waiting another opportunity to rise above her status. She would make a tumultuous but ruthless $pod_Embrace$ candidate and now that she's nobody again, is the time to move."
+ podgreatpersons.0234.desc: "Yong-deok was born a [Glossary('nobi','podgloss.nobi')|l] and worked as a palace lady before catching the eye of King U of the Goryeo. Quickly becoming a Royal Consort, she played the few cards she had well to maintain influence on King U, despite his interests in other #italic nobi#!.\nWhile U was trying to use the rise of the Ming to remove Goryeo from the Chinese dominion, Yong-deok lost his favor, was accused of plotting and was banished from court. Her family was executed and their body publicly displayed.\nBut the King had a fickle mind and ambition, leading him to push against the Ming despite the wishes of his advisor council. He will quickly change his mind regarding Yong-deok and he will reinstate and pardon her.\nKing U will fall eventually, and Yong-deok will be removed from the court, going back to be a #italic nobi#!, awaiting another opportunity to rise above her status. She would make a tumultuous but ruthless $pod_Embrace$ candidate and now that she's nobody again, it's the time to move."
  podgreatpersons.0235.t: "Yi Hye-bi"
- podgreatpersons.0235.desc: "When the consort of King Gongmin, failing to produce an heir, asked him to choose a concubine, King Gongmin chose the daughter of the poet philosopher Yi Che-hyǒn. The King had surrounded himself with the [Glossary('jajewi','podgloss.jajewi')|l] and focused more on his arts than on his wives and concubine, leading people to believe he was impotent.\nGongmin, desperate for an heir, and unable to produce one on his own, ordered the #italic jajewi#! to rape his concubines in order for him to claim a potential child as his own.\nThis order, with the threat of the #italic jajewi#! of being executed once a concubine was pregnant, led to the #italic jajewi#! to assainate King Gongmin, freeing Yi Hye-bi of her oblication.\nShe shaved her head and retired to a buddhist monastery, leaving an extended life, witnessing the fall of Goryo and the rise of the Joseon.\nHer old age is catching up, and if you want to $pod_Embrace$ that witness of Korean history, your retainers told you that she does have long left to live."
