  podgreatpersons.0236.t: "Park Paeng-nyeon"
- podgreatpersons.0236.desc: "Scholar of the Joseon dynasty, appointed to the Hall of Worthies, Paeng-nyeon formalised the Korean alphabet and participated in the creation of the [Glossary('Hunminjeongeum','podgloss.hunminjeongeum')], under the patronage of King Sejong the Great.\nNominated to higher function by King Danjong, Paeng-nyeon refused to acknowledge King Sejo when he overthrew Danjong. Despite his participation in a plot to restore Danjong, King Sejo offered a pardon to Paeng-nyeon if he denied his involvment in the coup and recognized King Sejo authority. Facing the refusal of Park Paeng-nyeon, who got to extra length to not recognize the authority of the King by his clever uses of the language he helped creating, King Sejo imprisoned Park Paeng-nyeon to torture him.\nYour agents have come with a plot to escape him from prison, if you were to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ the disgraced scholar."
+ podgreatpersons.0236.desc: "A scholar of the Joseon dynasty, appointed to the Hall of Worthies, Paeng-nyeon formalised the Korean alphabet and participated in the creation of the [Glossary('Hunminjeongeum','podgloss.hunminjeongeum')] under the patronage of King Sejong the Great.\nNominated to higher office by King Danjong, Paeng-nyeon refused to acknowledge King Sejo when he overthrew Danjong. Despite his participation in a plot to restore Danjong, King Sejo offered a pardon to Paeng-nyeon if he denied his involvment in the coup and recognized King Sejo's authority. Facing the refusal of Park Paeng-nyeon, who went to extra lengths to not recognize the authority of the King by his clever uses of the language he helped creating, King Sejo imprisoned Park Paeng-nyeon to torture him.\nYour agents have come with a plot to escape him from prison, if you were to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ the disgraced scholar."
  podgreatpersons.0237.t: "Park Gu-ma"
- podgreatpersons.0237.desc: "The Joseon dynasty introduced Confucian gender segregation, leading to increasing severity in the persecution of women. One of those, Park Gu-ma, has been forced to divorce Prince Taegang after an adultery case.\nShe used the opportunity to express herself through dance and poem, becoming famous. Her beauty, quick wit, charm and intelligence were remarked by everyone, especially by men of all standing. But what reached your ears are not her poems. It's the news of her trial for adultery, involving firty two men, from princes to slaves and especially how whe staid proud, fierce and unapologetic during her ordeal.\nThe sentence in those case are, usually, to be turned into a [Glossary('kisaeng', 'podgloss.kisaeng')]. But you could use your influence on court official to have her sentenced to death instead, allowing you to snatch her and $pod_Embrace$ her."
+ podgreatpersons.0237.desc: "The Joseon dynasty introduced Confucian gender segregation, leading to increasing severity in the persecution of women. One of those, Park Gu-ma, has been forced to divorce Prince Taegang after an adultery case.\nShe used the opportunity to express herself through dance and poem, becoming famous. Her beauty, quick wit, charm and intelligence were remarked on by everyone, especially by men of all standing. But what reached your ears are not her poems. It's the news of her trial for adultery, involving fifty two men, from princes to slaves and especially how she stood proud, fierce and unapologetic during her ordeal.\nThe sentence in such cases is, usually, to be turned into a [Glossary('kisaeng', 'podgloss.kisaeng')]. But you could use your influence on court officials to have her sentenced to \"death\" instead, allowing you to snatch her and $pod_Embrace$ her."
  podgreatpersons.0238.t: "Jo Gwang-jo"
- podgreatpersons.0238.desc: "Born into the Hungu faction, Jo Gwang-jo has faced a lot of adversity for his interests and study of neo-confucianism, a tenet of the Sarim faction, opposing the Hungu in their struggle to control the destiny of Joseon. Exiled during the second [Glossary('sahwa', 'podgloss.sahwa')|l], he lived as a [Glossary('seonbi', 'podgloss.seonbi')|l] before returning to court to enter the Royal Academy of Seonggyungwan once King Yeonsangun has been deposed.\nJo Gwang-jo quickly obtained the unconditional trust of King Jungjong and, after graduating, started to work on reforming the Joseon administration, codifying the hyangyak and setting up a new graduation system focusing not only on knowledge but also on common sense.\nThat last one will allow for the Hungu to get back in power, which will lead to the exile of the scholar during the third #italic sahwa#!, after they drew a wedge between the King and Gwang-jo.\nExiled, and sentenced to death by poison, Gwang-jo still hope for the good will of King Jungjong, leaving is north door always opened. Your contacts told you that the soldier tasked with delivering him the poison are en-route. Now is the time to decide if you want to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ the scholar."
+ podgreatpersons.0238.desc: "Born into the Hungu faction, Jo Gwang-jo has faced a lot of adversity for his interests and study of neo-confucianism, a tenet of the Sarim faction, opposing the Hungu in their struggle to control the destiny of Joseon. Exiled during the second [Glossary('sahwa', 'podgloss.sahwa')|l], he lived as a [Glossary('seonbi', 'podgloss.seonbi')|l] before returning to court to enter the Royal Academy of Seonggyungwan once King Yeonsangun had been deposed.\nJo Gwang-jo quickly obtained the unconditional trust of King Jungjong and, after graduating, started to work on reforming the Joseon administration, codifying the hyangyak and setting up a new graduation system focusing not only on knowledge but also on common sense.\nThat last one will allow for the Hungu to get back in power, which will lead to the exile of the scholar during the third #italic sahwa#!, after they drove a wedge between the King and Gwang-jo.\nExiled, and sentenced to death by poison, Gwang-jo still hopes for the goodwill of King Jungjong, leaving his north door always opened. Your contacts told you that the soldiers tasked with delivering him the poison are en-route. Now is the time to decide if you want to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ the scholar."
  podgreatpersons.0239.t: "Yi Sun-sin"
- podgreatpersons.0239.desc: "Entering a military career, Yi Sun-sin started by fending of Jurchen incursion against the border, during which he quickly gathered a reputation for his strategic and leadership skills. Soon enough, he was promoted commander of the Left Jeolla Naval District, which allowed him to start the buildup of the navy. That effort culminated when he engineered the [Glossary('geobukseon', 'podgloss.geobukseon')|l].\nWhen the Japanese finally started the Imjin War to invade Korea, Yi Sun-sin relentlessly pushed them back again and again, trying to preserve has much of his troops and boats than possible, gaining a reputation of folk hero, standing up against the Japanese, while King Seonjo was perceived as incapable.\nYi Sun-sin has been critically wounded during the battle of Noryand, during which he managed to sunk and capture almost the entirety of the Japanese fleet, while being outnumbered two to one. According to your agents there is a short window of opportunity, amidst the chaos of the battle, and you can try to $pod_Embrace$ the Chungmu-gong before he let out his last breath."
+ podgreatpersons.0239.desc: "Entering a military career, Yi Sun-sin started by fending off Jurchen incursions against the border, during which he quickly gathered a reputation for his strategic and leadership skills. Soon enough, he was promoted commander of the Left Jeolla Naval District, which allowed him to start the buildup of the navy. That effort culminated when he engineered the [Glossary('geobukseon', 'podgloss.geobukseon')|l].\nWhen the Japanese finally started the Imjin War to invade Korea, Yi Sun-sin relentlessly pushed them back again and again, trying to preserve as much of his troops and boats as possible, gaining a reputation as a folk hero standing up against the Japanese, while King Seonjo was perceived as incapable.\nYi Sun-sin has been critically wounded during the battle of Noryand, during which he managed to sink and capture almost the entirety of the Japanese fleet, while being outnumbered two to one. According to your agents there is a short window of opportunity, amidst the chaos of the battle, and you can try to $pod_Embrace$ the Chungmu-gong before he lets out his last breath."
  podgreatpersons.0240.t: "Kwak Chaeu"
- podgreatpersons.0240.desc: "Unable to pass the examination for civil service, due to his harsh position against the government, Kwak Chaeu went into hiding, waiting for an opportunity. When the Japanese started the Imjin war, he started assembling a righteous army of irregulars and, using unconventional tactics, he managed to slaughter the invaders while they tried to cross the Nam River.\nRecognising his effort, and trying to buy popular approval, King Seonjo, granted him an official capacity soon after his victory. He led numerous other battle with his righteous ary, wearing his emblematic Red Robe, leading the battles from the frontline.\nHe survived the war unscathed. His opponents affirm that it's due to his Red Robe that he allegedly doused in menstrual virgin blood, providing him with enough Yin to absorb the Yan of their bullets. Wether this is true or not, it did raised your interest.\nEnjoying a calm and secluded life, having packed his Red Robe days away, Kwak Chaeu know awaits death without fear."
+ podgreatpersons.0240.desc: "Unable to pass the examination for civil service due to his harsh position against the government, Kwak Chaeu went into hiding, waiting for an opportunity. When the Japanese started the Imjin war, he started assembling a righteous army of irregulars and, using unconventional tactics, he managed to slaughter the invaders while they tried to cross the Nam River.\nRecognising his efforts, and trying to buy popular approval, King Seonjo granted him an official capacity soon after his victory. He led numerous other battles with his righteous army, wearing his emblematic Red Robe and leading the battles from the frontline.\nHe survived the war unscathed. His opponents affirm that it's due to his Red Robe that he allegedly doused in menstrual virgin blood, providing him with enough Yin to absorb the Yang of their bullets. Wether this is true or not, it did raise your interest.\nEnjoying a calm and secluded life, having packed his Red Robe days away, Kwak Chaeu now awaits death without fear."
  podgreatpersons.0241.t: "Trân Thù Đô"
- podgreatpersons.0241.desc: "Architect of the rise of the Trân dynasty, Trân Thù Đô manipulated the child regnant queen Lý Chiêu Hoàng, married her to Trân Thái Tông, and made her abdicate for her husband, establishing the Trân dynasty to rule over the Đai Viêt.\nWhen Lý Chiêu Hoàng wasn't able to produce an heir, he forced Trân Liêu to give his pregnant wife, Princess Thuân Thiên, to the emperor, which prompted Tran Liâ to rebel against the royal family, made the emperor to retire as a monk over his feelings and lead to the execution of every soldier who rebelled once the emperor came back.\nSince then, he managed to repel a mongol invasion andremained busy with court business, even now that his life is declining. Now is the time to approach him and give him another whole clan to care for : Yours."
+ podgreatpersons.0241.desc: "The architect of the rise of the Trân dynasty, Trân Thù Đô manipulated the child regnant queen Lý Chiêu Hoàng, married her to Trân Thái Tông, and made her abdicate for her husband, establishing the Trân dynasty to rule over the Đai Viêt.\nWhen Lý Chiêu Hoàng wasn't able to produce an heir, he forced Trân Liêu to give his pregnant wife, Princess Thuân Thiên, to the emperor, which prompted Tran Liâ to rebel against the royal family, forced the emperor to retire as a monk over his feelings and led to the execution of every soldier who rebelled once the emperor came back.\nSince then, he managed to repel a mongol invasion and remained busy with court business, even now that his life is declining. Now is the time to approach him and give him another whole clan to care for: Yours."
  podgreatpersons.0242.t: "An Tu"
- podgreatpersons.0242.desc: "An Tu is one of the lady in waiting of the Trân dynasty. When the mongol invaded the Đai Viêt, routing the defender army, the imperial family tried to flee the capital on small boats, trying to lure the mongol away with their imperial ship. The invaders unraveled the hastely hatched plan and surrounded the fleet.\nThe emperor Trân Thánh Tông had to rely on another trick. Using the natural beauty of An Tu, he offered her to Toghon, son of Kubilai Khan, leader of the invader, passing her as one of the Trân Princess. The beauty of An Tu, with a note of despair, helped selling the story and gave enough tinme for the Trân armies to regroup and slaughter the Mongols.\nWhat happens to An Tu during the battle is a strange story, that your retainer is trying to sell you, as they got their hand on the Princess of precious leaves and branches."
+ podgreatpersons.0242.desc: "An Tu is one of the ladies-in-waiting of the Trân dynasty. When the Mongols invaded the Đai Viêt, routing the defending army, the imperial family tried to flee the capital on small boats, trying to lure the Mongols away with their imperial ship. The invaders unraveled the hastily hatched plan and surrounded the fleet.\nThe emperor Trân Thánh Tông had to rely on another trick. Using the natural beauty of An Tu, he offered her to Toghon, son of Kubilai Khan, leader of the invaders, passing her off as one of the Trân Princesses. The beauty of An Tu, with a note of despair, helped selling the story and gave enough time for the Trân armies to regroup and slaughter the Mongols.\nAn Tu's fate after the battle is unknown, already the subject of many strange and conflicting stories. You could use this chaos as an opportunity to get your hands on this \"Princess of Precious Leaves and Branches\"."
  podgreatpersons.0243.t: "Trân Húng Đao"
- podgreatpersons.0243.desc: "Son of Prince Trân Liêu, who had to cede his wife to the child emperor Trân Thai Tông, Trân Húng Đao started a military carreer, that would lead him to become one of the most successful general of the Đai Viêt.\nSurviving the first mongol invasion, as a border officer, he was at the head of the combined land and naval forces of the Đai Viêt during the second mongol invasion of the Đai Viêt. Despite severe loss, and due to the climate and sickness rampaging amongst the Mongol, he managed to repel the invaders over the Red River.\nTwo years later, Kublai Khan send his favorite son, Prince Toghan, to invade the Đai Viêt. Once again, they were met with fierce resistance and routed by the tactical genius of Trân Húng Đao, who manage to trap and destroy four hundreds mongols ships in the Bach Đang River.\nNow retired, the illness of the great general has come to your ears. If you want to $pod_Embrace$ him you should do it before it's too late."
+ podgreatpersons.0243.desc: "After having to cede his wife to the child emperor Trân Thai Tông, Trân Húng Đao started a military career that would lead him to become one of the most successful generals of the Đai Viêt.\nSurviving the first Mongol invasion as a border officer, he was at the head of the combined land and naval forces of the Đai Viêt during the second Mongol invasion. Despite severe losses, and due to the hostile climate and sickness running rampant amongst the Mongols, he managed to repel the invaders over the Red River.\nTwo years later, Kublai Khan sent his favorite son, Prince Toghan, to invade the Đai Viêt. Once again, they were met with fierce resistance and were routed by the tactical genius of Trân Húng Đao, who managed to trap and destroy four hundred Mongol ships in the Bach Đang River.\nNow retired, news of the illness of the great general has reached your ears. If you want to $pod_Embrace$ him you should do it before it's too late."
  podgreatpersons.0244.t: "Lê Van Huu"
- podgreatpersons.0244.desc: "Born of humble origin, Lê Van Huu proved to be a very comptent scholar, ranking in second position in the Imperial examination at only seventeen. From there he was appointed a court official, a member of the Hanlin academy, and finally got in charge of the royal office for historical records.\nBenefitting from his access to those record, he started compiling them into a comprehensive historical book of the Đai Viêt. A thirty [Glossary('quyên','podgloss.guyen')|l] long book, the #italic Đai Viêt su ky!# is a comprehensive reccounting of the Đai Viet, intended to establish the empire as always being independant and equal to China. His writing are now used to reinforce the legitimcay of the Tran dynasty currently in power.\nNow retired and close to a century year old, the frail man has retired himself in his house, waiting for death to come. But letting such a mind to disappear forever would be a shame, and you could $pod_Embrace$ him."
+ podgreatpersons.0244.desc: "Born of humble origins, Lê Van Huu proved to be a very competent scholar, ranking in second place at the Imperial examination at only seventeen. From there, he was appointed as a court official, a member of the Hanlin academy, and finally got in charge of the royal office for historical records.\nBenefitting from his access to those records, he started compiling them into a comprehensive historical book of the Đai Viêt. A thirty [Glossary('quyên','podgloss.guyen')|l] long book, the #italic Đai Viêt su ky!# is a comprehensive recounting of the Đai Viet, intended to establish the empire as always being independent and equal to China. His writings are now used to reinforce the legitimcay of the Tran dynasty currently in power.\nNow retired and close to a century old, the frail man has retired himself in his house, waiting for death to come. But letting such a mind disappear forever would be a shame, and you could $pod_Embrace$ him."
  podgreatpersons.0245.t: "Huyên Trân"
- podgreatpersons.0245.desc: "Daughter of the retired Emperor Tran Nhân Tông, Huyên Trân was used by his brother as a bargaining chip to secure a diplomatic expansion plan and a political alliance with the Kingdom of Champa and married her to King Jaya Simhavarman III.\nBarely one year later, King Jaya died in mysterious circumstances. Refusing to be cremated with her late husband, as is the local custom, she sent for a man who was suspected to be her lover to come and rescue her.\nThe daring and extravagant scheme succeeded and the lovers disappeared without a trace.\nMore importantly, one of your agent managed to secure a place in the expedition and can get rid of the lover if you would want to gift that daring poetess with the gift of $pod_Embrace$."
+ podgreatpersons.0245.desc: "A daughter of the retired Emperor Tran Nhân Tông, Huyên Trân was used by his brother as a bargaining chip to secure a diplomatic expansion plan and a political alliance with the Kingdom of Champa, marrying her off to King Jaya Simhavarman III.\nBarely one year later, King Jaya died in mysterious circumstances. Refusing to be cremated with her late husband, as is the local custom, she sent for a man who was suspected to be her lover to come and rescue her.\nThe daring and extravagant scheme succeeded and the lovers disappeared without a trace.\nMore importantly, one of your agents managed to secure a place in the expedition, and can get rid of the lover if you would want to offer that daring poetess the gift of the $pod_Embrace$."
  podgreatpersons.0246.t: "Mac Đinh Chi"
- podgreatpersons.0246.desc: "Despite his frail body and ugliness, Mac Đinh Chi brillantly passed the imperial examination and became the youngest to reach the title of [Glossary('Thai Hoc Sinh','podgloss.thai_hoc_sinh')]. His wits, integrity and mastery of poetry to convey his point managed to impress the Emperor Trân Minh Tông.\nHis successors used Mac Đinh Chi skills to lead two diplomatic missions with the Yuan dynasty. His travels left a long lasting impression amidst the Yuan, and allowed him to approach and tie strong bounds with the Goryeo diplomats, in particular with the niece of the ambassador, whom he married.\nThe life of the poet-scholar is now ending, retired from the court. If he would to disappear in a strange accident, Đai Viêt would not lose much, but you would gain a lot."
+ podgreatpersons.0246.desc: "Despite his frail body and ugliness, Mac Đinh Chi brillantly passed the imperial examination and became the youngest to reach the title of [Glossary('Thai Hoc Sinh','podgloss.thai_hoc_sinh')]. His wits, integrity and mastery of poetry to convey his arguments managed to impress the Emperor Trân Minh Tông.\nHis successors used Mac Đinh Chi's skills to lead two diplomatic missions with the Yuan dynasty. His travels left a long-lasting impression amidst the Yuan, and allowed him to approach and tie strong bonds with Goryeo diplomats, in particular with the niece of the ambassador, whom he married.\nThe life of the poet-scholar is now ending, retired from court. If he were to disappear in a strange accident, Đai Viêt would not lose much, but you would gain a lot."
  podgreatpersons.0247.t: "Nga Tet Pya"
- podgreatpersons.0247.desc: "During the unification of the Sagaing and Pinya kingdom in the Kingdom of Ava, following the brutal raids of the Shan Maw, Tet Pya used the fact that the new king was frequently on the road to fight rebel to make a name for himself. Picking high profile target, he led a campaign of heist and robberies along the Irrawaddy river. Evading capture for a while, he finally got arrested in 1366 by King Thado Minbya's men.\nWhen asked by the King what weapon he should use to execute him, he famously answered #italic I chose your most beautiful queen, Saw Omma#!. Which triggered the most unexpected answer from the cruel and brutal king, who offered him a commanding post in his army.\nHis protector just died, forcing him to flee the court in hiding, to the desperation of numerous servants and princess who long for his embrace. Your servants have found a way to reach him, if you wish to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ him."
+ podgreatpersons.0247.desc: "During the unification of the Sagaing and Pinya kingdoms in the Kingdom of Ava, following the brutal raids of the Shan Maw, Tet Pya used the fact that the new king was frequently on the road to fight rebels to make a name for himself. Picking high profile targets, he led a campaign of heists and robberies along the Irrawaddy river. Evading capture for a while, he finally got arrested in 1366 by King Thado Minbya's men.\nWhen asked by the King what weapon he should use to execute him, he famously answered #italic I chose your most beautiful queen, Saw Omma#!. Which triggered the most unexpected answer from the cruel and brutal king, who offered him a commanding post in his army.\nHis protector just died, forcing him to flee the court in hiding, to the desperation of numerous servants and princesses who long for his embrace. Your servants have found a way to reach him, if you wish to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ him."
  podgreatpersons.0248.t: "Piya Yaza Dewi"
- podgreatpersons.0248.desc: "Born a commoner, Mwei Manet started her life by selling flowers in Dagon, when the rebel Prince Binnya Nwe saw her and fell under her spell, taking her as a wife against everyone else advice. The first wife of the Prince, Tala Mi Daw, was deeply hurt by the obsession of the Prince with Mwei Manet.\nWhen the King Binnya U of Pegu died, the nobles invited the prince in exile to come back to rule the kingdom but the spell the Prince was under was so strong that Mi Daw refused to be coronated with him as long as Yaza Dewi would remain. Strengthening her hold on the king, Yaza Dewi became queen and pushed Tala Mi Daw to kill herself out of desperation. She also suggested to Binnya Nwe that he should execute his only son, Balawkyantaw.\nHer luck, or her spells, are running out and she found herself entangled in an assassination plot against her. You could pull the rug under her assassins footing and $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her."
+ podgreatpersons.0248.desc: "Born a commoner, Mwei Manet started her life by selling flowers in Dagon, when the rebel Prince Binnya Nwe saw her and fell under her spell, taking her as a wife against his court's wishes. The first wife of the Prince, Tala Mi Daw, was deeply hurt by the obsession of the Prince with Mwei Manet.\nWhen the King Binnya U of Pegu died, the nobles invited the prince in exile to come back to rule the kingdom, but the spell the Prince was under was so strong that Mi Daw refused to be coronated with him as long as Yaza Dewi would remain. Strengthening her hold on the king, Yaza Dewi became queen and pushed Tala Mi Daw to kill herself out of desperation. She also suggested to Binnya Nwe that he should execute his only son, Balawkyantaw.\nHer luck, or her spells, are running out and she found herself entangled in an assassination plot against her. You could pull the rug under her assassins and $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her instead."
  podgreatpersons.0249.t: "Đang Dung"
- podgreatpersons.0249.desc: "Under the Ho dynasty, Đang Dung helped his father to govern Thuân Hoa. When the Ming army came and occupied the country, ending the Ho dynasty, he joined the insurrection started by the Trân dynasty and helped securing the throne for Trân Ngoi.\nRealising that the Emperor was manipulated by his eunuchs, Đang Dung, once again, entered rebellion and deposed Trân Ngoi, which allowed his friend Trân Quy Khoáng to take the throne. Peace din't last and the Ming invaded the kingdom, inflicting severe defeat at great costs to the armies led by Đan Dung. Not willing to surrender, he led a losing campaign of resistance against the invader for years, before his emperor was captured and killed.\nYour agents, following the trail of the brilliant general, warned you that he wrote a death poem and that he may take his life in solidarity with his friend. $pod_Embrace$ him now, or take the risk of losing the brilliant mind of the poet general."
+ podgreatpersons.0249.desc: "Under the Ho dynasty, Đang Dung helped his father to govern Thuân Hoa. When the Ming army came and occupied the country, ending the Ho dynasty, he joined the insurrection started by the Trân dynasty and helped securing the throne for Trân Ngoi.\nRealising that the Emperor was manipulated by his eunuchs, Đang Dung once again rebelled and deposed Trân Ngoi, which allowed his friend Trân Quy Khoáng to take the throne. Peace didn't last and the Ming invaded the kingdom, inflicting severe defeats at great cost to the armies led by Đan Dung. Not willing to surrender, he led a losing campaign of resistance against the invaders for years, before his emperor was captured and killed.\nYour agents, following the trail of the brilliant general, warned you that he wrote a death poem and that he may take his life in solidarity with his friend. $pod_Embrace$ him now, or take the risk of losing the brilliant mind of the poet general."
  podgreatpersons.0250.t: "Keo Phimpha"
- podgreatpersons.0250.desc: "For the last decade, the kingdom of Lan Xang has been the theater of so many faction war that it's been hard for you keep track of them all. Following the death of Lan Kham Deng a succession crisis got out of hand, leading to the assassination of, at least, seven different kings in less than ten years.\nAnd the mastermind behind all of this seems to be the old Keo Phimpha. Her motivations are known only to herself, but her determination knows no bounds.\nAntagonising the court, however, did lead to her arrest and planned execution, tied to her husband and left to be eaten by the naga.\nThe dangerous and bitter old lady will probably adapt very well to eternal life, if you decided to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her."
+ podgreatpersons.0250.desc: "For the last decade, the kingdom of Lan Xang has been the theater of so many faction wars that it's been hard for you keep track of them all. Following the death of Lan Kham Deng, a succession crisis got out of hand, leading to the assassination of at least seven different kings in less than ten years.\nAnd the mastermind behind all of this seems to be the old Keo Phimpha. Her motivations are known only to herself, but her determination knows no bounds.\nAntagonising the court, however, did lead to her arrest and planned execution, tied to her husband and left to be eaten by the naga.\nThe dangerous and bitter old lady will probably adapt very well to eternal life, if you decided to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her."
  podgreatpersons.0251.t: "Trinh Kha"
- podgreatpersons.0251.desc: "Close friend and advisor of Lê Loi, Trinh Kha was instrumental in the rebellion against the Ming dynasty and the restoration of the Đai Viêt as an independant realm gaining the title of [Glossary('Hành khiên', 'podgloss.hanh_khien')]. Sent away during the regency following the death of his friend, he plotted to secure a position as sole the power behind the throne, disposing of an entranched regent.\nWhen the young king died, Queen Nguyen Thi Anh became regent for the infant Lê Nhân Tông. Trinh Kha managed to manipulate the relatively young regent and shared power with her.\nThat is up until recently. He's now emprisoned and await for his execution. Your agents heards rumors about Trinh Kha trying to force himself onto the Queen, but no official reason has been given for his disgrace.\nIf you want to get the advisor and skilled schemer for yourself, you should act now."
+ podgreatpersons.0251.desc: "A close friend and advisor of Lê Loi, Trinh Kha was instrumental in the rebellion against the Ming dynasty and the restoration of the Đai Viêt as an independent realm, gaining the title of [Glossary('Hành khiên', 'podgloss.hanh_khien')]. Sent away during the regency following the death of his friend, he plotted to secure a position as the sole power behind the throne, disposing of an entrenched regent.\nWhen the young king died, Queen Nguyen Thi Anh became regent for the infant Lê Nhân Tông. Trinh Kha managed to manipulate the relatively young regent and shared power with her.\nThat is up until recently. He's now imprisoned and awaits his execution. Your agents heard rumors about Trinh Kha trying to force himself onto the Queen, but no official reason has been given for his disgrace.\nIf you want to get this advisor and skilled schemer for yourself, you should act now."
  podgreatpersons.0252.t: "Shin Sawbu"
- podgreatpersons.0252.desc: "Born a daughter in a turbulent family of monarch, she was kidnapped to marry the King of Ava during a succession crisis involving her brothers. She stayed in a monastery after the death of her husband and managed to return to Pegu thanks to the help of two monk.\nAfter all of the male member of her family had managed to kill each others, she found herself to be sitting on the throne, inaugurating a long period of peace and stability in the kingdom.\nFeeling the call of the monastery, she abdicated seven years later in favor of one of the monk who helped her escaping Ava and moved to the buddhist [Glossary('stûpa','podgloss.stupa')|l] of Shwedagon where she ruled as a monk queen. The [Glossary('Binnya Thau', 'podgloss.binnya_thau')] is awaiting for the next cycle of the wheel to take her, but you could get one of the few queen of the area for your own plots. "
+ podgreatpersons.0252.desc: "Born a daughter in a turbulent family of monarchs, Shin Sawbu was kidnapped to marry the King of Ava during a succession crisis involving her brothers. She stayed in a monastery after the death of her husband and managed to return to Pegu thanks to the help of two monks.\nAfter all of the male members of her family had managed to kill each other, she found herself sitting on the throne, inaugurating a long period of peace and stability in the kingdom.\nFeeling the call of the monastery again, she abdicated seven years later in favor of one of the monks who helped her escaping Ava and moved to the buddhist [Glossary('stûpa','podgloss.stupa')|l] of Shwedagon where she ruled as a monk queen. The [Glossary('Binnya Thau', 'podgloss.binnya_thau')] is waiting for the next cycle of the wheel to take her, but you could get one of the few queens of the area for your own plots."
  podgreatpersons.0253.t: "Yazathingyan"
- podgreatpersons.0253.desc: "Yazathingyan served successfully seven kings of Ava during an eventful life of service as a military officer and advisor. Starting his career during the forty years wars between Ava and Hanthawaddy he then led a successful expansion campaign, survived the succession crisis of the Mohnyi rebellion and showed is value to the new king by advising him during the Ava civil war, up until the eccentricity of the king showed to be too much for him.\nHe supported the new king to re-establish Ava's dominion over former vassal, by force, and finally, repelled a Chinese invasion.\nBut he's king has been stabbed in the palace, under his supervision, and he couldn't save him. Now in disgrace, he retired, awaiting for a death that is finally coming. Either in the form of old age, or by your hand, if you were to $pod_Embrace$ him."
+ podgreatpersons.0253.desc: "Yazathingyan served seven kings of Ava during an eventful life of service as a military officer and advisor. Starting his career during the forty year wars between Ava and Hanthawaddy, he then led a successful expansion campaign, survived the succession crisis of the Mohnyi rebellion, and showed is value to the new king by advising him during the Ava civil war, up until the eccentricity of the king proved to be too much for him.\nHe supported the new king to re-establish Ava's dominion over its former vassals by force, and finally, repelled a Chinese invasion.\nBut his king has been stabbed in the palace under his supervision, and he couldn't save him. Now in disgrace, he retired, waiting for a death that is finally coming. Either in the form of old age, or by your hand, if you were to $pod_Embrace$ him."
  podgreatpersons.0254.t: "Diogo Soares"
- podgreatpersons.0254.desc: "The adventures of Diogo Soares are nearing an end with the the death of Tabinshwehti, King and founder of the Toungoo Empire. He died due to his alcooholism, that was brought unto him by the Portuguese 'explorer'.\nBanished from India for his murederous and privateer carreer, Soares landed in Burma due to bad weather. There he rapidly met and befriended Tabinshwehti, who made him general during the Shwehti war, with disastrous consequences.\nHis last bender, kidnapping the daughter of a rich merchant during her marriage to marry her, killing everyone who tried to rescue her just to have the bride commit suicide, is the reason for his arrest by Tabinshwehti successor.\nHis house is on fire, his riches are looted by an angry mob, and if you want to get this connoisseur of fine wine, you should move fast to $pod_Embrace$ him."
+ podgreatpersons.0254.desc: "The adventures of Diogo Soares are nearing an end with the the death of Tabinshwehti, King and founder of the Toungoo Empire. He died due to his alcoholism that was brought unto him by the Portuguese 'explorers'.\nBanished from India for his murderous privateering career, Soares landed in Burma due to bad weather. There he rapidly met and befriended Tabinshwehti, who made him general during the Shwehti war, with disastrous consequences.\nHis last adventure, kidnapping the daughter of a rich merchant during her wedding to marry her, killing everyone who tried to rescue her just to have the bride commit suicide, is the reason for his arrest by Tabinshwehti's successor.\nHis house is on fire, his riches are looted by an angry mob, and if you want to get this connoisseur of fine wine, you should move fast to $pod_Embrace$ him."
  podgreatpersons.0255.t: "Nguyen Thi Lô"
- podgreatpersons.0255.desc: "Nguyen Tran is a confucian scholar, ruthless politician and master strategist who almost single handedly manage to get the Đai Viêt out of the dominion of the Ming, by advising and serving the future King Lê Loi.\nTired of the sycophantic and scheming of the court, he chose to retire in his country house, with his wives.\nHis second wife, Nguyen Thi Lô, was key in his strategies and one of his best advisor, as well as the tutor of the young King Lê Thai Tông. The King, wishing to pay a visit to his tutor and mistress, came to visit Nguyen Tran estate and curiously died the day after he arrived.\nNguyen Tran claim his innocence but has been sentenced to [Glossary('miezu','podgloss.miezu')|l]. You can't save such a high profile figure but Nguyen Thi Lô, the accused mistress, can be saved, if you could pay of some of her guards and decided to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her."
+ podgreatpersons.0255.desc: "Nguyen Tran is a confucian scholar, ruthless politician and master strategist who almost single-handedly managed to get the Đai Viêt out of the dominion of the Ming, by advising and serving the future King Lê Loi.\nTired of the sycophants and schemers at court, he chose to retire in his country house with his wives.\nHis second wife, Nguyen Thi Lô, was key in his strategies and one of his best advisors, as well as the tutor of the young King Lê Thai Tông. The King, wishing to pay a visit to his tutor and mistress, came to visit Nguyen Tran estate and curiously died the day after he arrived.\nNguyen Tran claims his innocence but has been sentenced to [Glossary('miezu','podgloss.miezu')|l]. You can't save such a high profile figure, but Nguyen Thi Lô, the accused mistress, can be saved, if you could pay off some of her guards and decided to $pod_Embrace$ or $pod_ghoul$ her."
  podgreatpersons.0256.t: "Tachibana Dōsetsu"
- podgreatpersons.0256.desc: "One of the fiercest warriors to walk the fields of Sengoku Kyushu, Tachibana Dōsetsu is a military prodigy who serves the Ōtomo clan with unwavering loyalty. Though half of his lower body was paralyzed later in his life, he still participated in 37 campaigns and over 100 smaller engagements. Dōsetsu is regarded as one of the wisest retainers of the Ōtomo. He organized an elite unit of 48 warriors, known as the “White Hawks”, personally trained and drilled under his strict code of discipline. Master of a unique and deadly sword style known as "the art of slashing in all directions", Dōsetsu is said to wield inhuman strength. He named his blade “Thousand Birds" until one day, lightning struck the tree he sheltered under. In a flash of instinct, he is said to have drawn his sword and cleaved the Thunder God inside the bolt, surviving what should have been certain death. Thereafter, he renamed his blade “Lightning Cutter.” There are rumours that Dōsetsu is currently dying of an illness, however. His death seems certain now, but an embrace could save the warrior, if you wished."
+ podgreatpersons.0256.desc: "One of the fiercest warriors to walk the fields of Sengoku Kyushu, Tachibana Dōsetsu is a military prodigy who serves the Ōtomo clan with unwavering loyalty. Though half of his lower body was paralyzed later in his life, he still participated in 37 campaigns and over 100 smaller engagements. He is regarded as one of the wisest retainers of the Ōtomo. He organized an elite unit of 48 warriors, known as the \"White Hawks\", personally trained and drilled under his strict code of discipline. Master of a unique and deadly sword style known as [Glossary('tachiuchi ni myō o etaru', 'podgloss.tachiuchi_ni_myo_o_etaru')], Dōsetsu is said to wield inhuman strength. He named his blade [Glossary('Chidori', 'podgloss.chidori')] until one day, lightning struck the tree he sheltered under. In a flash of instinct, he is said to have drawn his sword and cleaved the Thunder God inside the bolt, surviving what should have been certain death. Thereafter, he renamed his blade [Glossary('Raikiri', 'podgloss.raikiri')]. There are rumours that Dōsetsu is currently dying of an illness, however. His death seems certain now, but an $pod_Embrace$ could save the warrior, if you so wished."
  podgreatpersons.0257.t: "Ikkyū"
- podgreatpersons.0257.desc: "Illegitimate son of Emperor Go-Komatsu and a lowborn woman, Ikkyū was raised in monastic life from age five. He studied at Kyoto’s Ankoku-ji, then moved to Daitoku-ji, where he became a brilliant but volatile disciple of Zen. He rejected institutional Buddhism, condemning the corruption he saw in temples. Chose wandering, sake, and poetry over robes and incense. He achieved kenshō, sudden enlightenment, while listening to a crow caw in a boat on Lake Biwa. Afterwards, he taught Zen through passion and mockery. He slept with courtesans, especially a blind singer named Mori, whom he fell in love with. Now, Ikkyū has returned to Daitoku-ji, late in his life. Clearly in his final days, the monk lies with fevered breath, awaiting death. Your embrace could save the mad monk, and maybe in your court, he will find a place."
+ podgreatpersons.0257.desc: "The illegitimate son of Emperor Go-Komatsu and a lowborn woman, Ikkyū was raised in a monastic lifestyle from age five. He studied at Kyoto’s Ankoku-ji, then moved to Daitoku-ji, where he became a brilliant but volatile disciple of Zen. He rejected institutional Buddhism, condemning the corruption he saw in temples. He chose wandering, sake, and poetry over robes and incense. He achieved [Glossary('kenshō', 'podgloss.kensho')] while listening to a crow caw in a boat on Lake Biwa. Afterwards, he taught Zen through passion and mockery. He slept with courtesans, especially a blind singer named Mori, whom he fell in love with. Now, Ikkyū has returned to Daitoku-ji, late in his life. Clearly in his final days, the monk lies with fevered breath, awaiting death. Your $pod_Embrace$ could save the mad monk, and maybe in your court, he will find a place."
  podgreatpersons.0258.t: "Kō no Moronao"
- podgreatpersons.0258.desc: "A samurai from the Kō clan, Moronao rose through brilliance. As steward to Ashikaga Takauji, he gained much influence in the imperial court. This sparked the bloody and divisive Kannō Disturbance, a civil war with very serious repercussions for the whole country. Moronao purged enemies with fury and ruthlessness until a truce was agreed upon with the help of a Zen master who was close to both sides. Despised by nobles and monks alike, he was finally forced into retirement. Lately you have heard some credible rumours that the Uesugi clan is planning on executing the man. You could simply ignore this defeated warrior and leave him to his fate, or grant him another chance in your court."
+ podgreatpersons.0258.desc: "A samurai from the Kō clan, Moronao rose the ranks through brilliance. As steward to Ashikaga Takauji, he gained much influence in the imperial court. This sparked the bloody and divisive Kannō Disturbance, a civil war with very serious repercussions for the whole country. Moronao purged enemies with fury and ruthlessness until a truce was agreed upon with the help of a Zen master who was close to both sides. Despised by nobles and monks alike, he was finally forced into retirement.\nLately you have heard some credible rumours that the Uesugi clan is planning on executing the man. You could simply ignore this defeated warrior and leave him to his fate, or grant him another chance in your court."
  podgreatpersons.0259.t: "Ben no Naishi"
- podgreatpersons.0259.desc: "Daughter of a painter and poet, Ben no Naishi rose to the imperial court with grace. She served Emperor Go-Fukakusa as naishi-no-kami, entrusted with sacred rites and the divine regalia itself. She has recorded palace life in skilled brushstrokes, giving many a window in the royal world. More than a scribe, she was a counselor, a keeper of beauty. However, quite abruptly, she seems to have disappeared from court after the emperor's abdication. Some say she has chosen a quiet retirement, others think of darker possibilities. Whatever the truth may be, finding this court lady should be possible, if you pulled some strings."
