  junius_alim_modifier_desc: "Junius has an unmatched knowledge of Islamic law and tradition outside the Ashirra. This has earned him a great deal of respect among the Islamic $pod_cainite$ world."
 
  podintroductions.322.t: "Turning the Tortoise"
- podintroductions.322.desc: "Northeast Asia has traditionally been the domain of the Black Tortoise Court of the $pod_kueijin$. Heavily influenced by the nomads it dwelt with, this Court has been having border conflicts with the Chinese Yellow Emperor Court for centuries, even more so since the Jurchen Jin dynasty started pushing south.\nThe heavily decentralized nature of the Black Tortoise is proving to be his downfall as the [Glossary('Yama Kings','podgloss.yamaking')]' influence has been growing steadily for a long while and $pod_akuma$ are now running rampant in the steppes. The $pod_cainites$ [Glossary('Anda','podgloss.anda')] following the Mongols proved to be the last nail on the coffin. The Black Tortoise Court now lies shattered, its center of power seemingly oblivious to its crumbling as it continues its petty skirmishes with the Yellow Emperor Court.\n\nThe main question remaining is which power will ultimately end the Tortoise's agony and rise to control the region?"
+ podintroductions.322.desc: "$TAB$Northeast Asia has traditionally been the domain of the [GetTitleByKey('e_andong').GetNameNoTier] of the $pod_kueijin$. Heavily influenced by the nomads it dwelt with, this Court has been having border conflicts with the Chinese [GetTitleByKey('h_china').GetNameNoTier] for centuries, even more so since the Jurchen Jin dynasty started pushing south.\n\n$TAB$The heavily decentralized nature of the Black Tortoise is proving to be his downfall as the [Glossary('Yama Kings','podgloss.yamaking')]' influence has been growing steadily for a long while and $pod_akuma$ are now running rampant in the steppes. The $pod_cainite$ [Glossary('Anda','podgloss.anda')] following the Mongols proved to be the last nail in the coffin. The Black Tortoise Court now lies shattered, its center of power seemingly oblivious to its crumbling as it continues its petty skirmishes with the Yellow Emperor Court.\n\n$TAB$The main question remaining is which power will ultimately end the Tortoise's agony and rise to control the region?"
  podintroductions.322.a: "A once great court's slow downfall."
   
  podintroductions.323.t: "Daimyos of the Night"
- podintroductions.323.desc: "On paper, Japan is part of the Azure Dragon Court of mainland $pod_kueijin$. De facto however, it has been doing its own thing for several centuries now.\nJapan vampires call themselves "Gaki" and are divided by clans, the Bishamon lead by Miura Yasutami being the dominant one at the moment. It also has the largest concentration of $pod_cainites$ in Asia though their political relevance is basically non existent.\n\nThe nightly rulers of Japan have been observing the collapse of the mainland courts with interest. Miura Yasutami is an advocate of waiting for their downfall to formally cut ties with them while others would like a more aggressive split. Whatever the method they end up choosing, Japanese $pod_kueijin$ seem poised to soon build their own court and become a considerable force in their own right.\nIt remains to be seen if the rival clans (and the estranged $pod_cainites$) will stay united after achieving this common goal."
+ podintroductions.323.desc: "$TAB$On paper, Japan is part of the [GetTitleByKey('e_goryeo').GetNameNoTier] of mainland $pod_kueijin$. De facto however, it has been doing its own thing for several centuries now.\n$TAB$Japan's vampires call themselves \"Gaki\" and are divided by clans, the [GetDynastyHouseByID('house_bishamon').GetName] led by [GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('795044').GetFirstName] being the dominant one at the moment. It also has the largest concentration of $pod_cainites$ in Asia, though their political relevance is basically nonexistent.\n\n$TAB$The nightly rulers of Japan have been observing the collapse of the mainland courts with interest. Miura Yasutami is an advocate of waiting for their downfall to formally cut ties with them, while others would like a more aggressive split. Whatever the method they end up choosing, Japanese $pod_kueijin$ seem poised to soon build their own court and become a considerable force in their own right.\n$TAB$It remains to be seen if the rival clans (and the estranged $pod_cainites$) will stay united after achieving this common goal."
  podintroductions.323.a: "Amaterasu's domain rises."
     
  podintroductions.324.t: "The Sleeping Dragon"
- podintroductions.324.desc: "Korea is the heart of the Azure Dragon Court, a political entity that is supposed to also oversee Japan. De facto, this hasn't been the case for centuries now and the Court has been sidelined as a dependent of the more powerful Chinese Yellow Emperor Court. Xiao, the latest Emperor "suggested" by the Chinese, is a shining example of a line of barely competent pawns.\n\nTimes are changing however as the Yellow Emperor Court falls more and more into decline. Ambitious Korean $pod_kueijin$ such as the (unrecognized) Ancestor of P'yong'yang Wang Kyu and the mysterious Soo-kyung Ahn are bidding their time and gathering strength. Xiao's time on the throne is likely to be short-lived but it remains unclear what will emerge from the Azure Dragon's fall and under which leadership."
+ podintroductions.324.desc: "$TAB$Korea is the heart of the [GetTitleByKey('e_goryeo').GetNameNoTier], a political entity that is supposed to also oversee Japan. De facto, this hasn't been the case for centuries now and the Court has been sidelined as a dependent of the more powerful Chinese [GetTitleByKey('h_china').GetNameNoTier]. [GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('793153').GetFirstName], the latest Emperor \"suggested\" by the Chinese, is a shining example of a line of barely competent pawns.\n\n$TAB$Times are changing however as the Yellow Emperor Court falls more and more into decline. Ambitious Korean $pod_kueijin$ such as the (unrecognized) Ancestor of P'yong'yang [GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('795046').GetFirstName] and the mysterious [GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('793174').GetFirstName] are biding their time and gathering strength. Xiao's time on the throne is likely to be short-lived, but it remains unclear what will emerge from the Azure Dragon's fall and under which leadership."
  podintroductions.324.a: "At the crossroads."
     
  podintroductions.325.t: "The Bloody Fall of the Phoenix"
- podintroductions.325.desc: "Southeast Asia was once home to the only Court rivaling China's Yellow Emperor Court, the Scarlet Phoenix. While said Court still technically exists, it has been reduced to very little because of centuries of indolence and a good dose of infighting. This power vacuum has let $pod_akuma$ take hold in most of the area and the Scarlet Phoenix Court now enjoys the dubious reputation of being an infernalist infested hellhole.\nThe Yellow Emperor Court itself has pondered direct intervention, something the fiercely independent [Glossary('Kuei-Jin','game_concept_kuei_jin_desc')] of the region would likely not allow easily.\n\nWhile most already consider the Scarlet Phoenix Court lost, rumors abound of a reclusive [Glossary('Bodhisattva','podgloss.bodhisattva')] named Piyau Payung recently coming out of the jungles to set things right.\nKnowing Piyau's "unique" philosophy however, most are wondering if the cure will be worse to endure than the disease..."
+ podintroductions.325.desc: "$TAB$Southeast Asia was once home to the only Court rivaling China's [GetTitleByKey('h_china').GetNameNoTier], the Scarlet Phoenix. While said Court still technically exists, it has been reduced to very little because of centuries of indolence and a good dose of infighting. This power vacuum has let $pod_akuma$ take hold in most of the area and the [GetTitleByKey('h_scarlet_phoenix_court').GetNameNoTier] now enjoys the dubious reputation of being an infernalist infested hellhole.\n$TAB$The Yellow Emperor Court itself has pondered direct intervention, something the fiercely independent [Glossary('Kuei-Jin','game_concept_kuei_jin_desc')] of the region would likely not allow easily.\n\n$TAB$While most already consider the Scarlet Phoenix Court lost, rumors abound of a reclusive [Glossary('Bodhisattva','podgloss.bodhisattva')] named [GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('791113').GetFirstName] recently coming out of the jungles to set things right.\n\n$TAB$Knowing Piyau's \"unique\" philosophy however, most are wondering if the cure will be worse to endure than the disease..."
  podintroductions.325.a: "A bloody reckoning is coming..."
  
  podintroductions.326.t: "All is Well Under Heaven"
- podintroductions.326.desc: "To the outside eye, the Yellow Emperor Court is still the pinnacle of the $pod_kueijin$ courts. It is unified under a wise leadership that promotes regional innovations, is unconcerned by mortal struggles and is running like a remainder of better days.\nThe truth, as always, is more complicated.\n\nThe Yellow Emperor is reclusive at best, a madman at worst. His incompetent sycophants are running the realm in his stead. The Jurchen courts of the North and the Song courts of the South are quietly plotting a schism. The [Glossary('Anda','podgloss.anda')] $pod_cainites$ are waiting for the right moment to follow their mortal counterparts' conquests. New heresies, some dangerously close to infernalism, are appearing unchecked everywhere.\n\nIt will take very little for Heaven to come crashing down on the fragile hegemon of China."
+ podintroductions.326.desc: "$TAB$To the outside eye, the [GetTitleByKey('h_china').GetNameNoTier] is still the pinnacle of the $pod_kueijin$ courts. It is unified under a wise leadership that promotes regional innovations, is unconcerned by mortal struggles, and is running like a reminder of better days.\n\n$TAB$The truth, as always, is more complicated.\n\n$TAB$The #ONCLICK:CHARACTER,[GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('795039').GetID] #TOOLTIP:CHARACTER,[GetScriptedCharacterByHistoryID('795039').GetID] #L Yellow Emperor#!#!#! is reclusive at best, a madman at worst. His incompetent sycophants are running the realm in his stead. The Jurchen courts of the North and the Song courts of the South are quietly plotting a schism. The [Glossary('Anda','podgloss.anda')] $pod_cainites$ are waiting for the right moment to follow their mortal counterparts' conquests. New heresies, some dangerously close to infernalism, are appearing unchecked everywhere.\n\n$TAB$It will take very little for Heaven to come crashing down on the fragile hegemon of China."
  podintroductions.326.a: "Long united..."
  
- podintroductions.327.desc: "Ambitious Wang Kyu, your bold schemes to take over Korea during your mortal life didn't bear fruit. Still, your death was merely a step in your inevitable ascension it seems. Returning as a $pod_kueijin$, you lost no time looking for opportunities to climb the immortal ladder.\nThe current chaos in P'yong'yang has claimed the life of the previous Ancestor and, before the Azure Dragon Court could react, you rose to the occasion and took the throne. While they haven't confirmed you, you have little concerns about the Court's reaction as, during your time there, you noticed that they are indolent and slow to react.\nThe true threat to your reign is much closer by, the self proclaimed rebel Hojil, burned to hell alongside his mentor Myoch'ong in 1136, came back and used his prestige to gather a following and claim P'yong'yang as his own.\nThis is your first hurdle to overcome and Hojil's removal will hopefully be a good first step to earn some legitimacy."
+ podintroductions.327.desc: "Ambitious Wang Kyu, your bold schemes to take over Korea during your mortal life didn't bear fruit. Still, your death was merely a step in your inevitable ascension it seems. Returning as a $pod_kueijin$, you lost no time looking for opportunities to climb the immortal ladder.\nThe current chaos in P'yong'yang has claimed the life of the previous Ancestor and, before the Azure Dragon Court could react, you rose to the occasion and took the throne. While they haven't confirmed you, you have little concerns about the Court's reaction as, during your time there, you noticed that they are indolent and slow to react.\nThe true threat to your reign is much closer by. The self proclaimed rebel Hojil, burned to hell alongside his mentor Myoch'ong in 1136, came back and used his prestige to gather a following and claim P'yong'yang as his own.\nThis is your first hurdle to overcome and Hojil's removal will hopefully be a good first step to earn some legitimacy."
  podintroductions.327.a: "I'm here to stay."
- wang_kyu_intro_tt: "As Wang Kyu, you start with very low legitimacy, something that can be solved by an unique decision."
+ wang_kyu_intro_tt: "As Wang Kyu, you start with very low legitimacy, something that can be solved by a unique decision."
  
  wang_kyu_decision: "Fated Master of Korea"
- wang_kyu_decision_desc: "Since your death the rules have changed but the goal hasn't. Korea will be yours, come what may. Securing your rule over P'yong'yang is the first step."
+ wang_kyu_decision_desc: "Since your death, the rules have changed but the goal hasn't. Korea will be yours, come what may. Securing your rule over P'yong'yang is the first step."
  wang_kyu_decision_tooltip: "Looking ahead."
