- podintroductions.334.desc: "General Li, times are changing. You were content living as a recluse far from the Court politics until a few decades back and now you are somehow the leader of a resistance group against [Glossary('Dokhor-Khan','podgloss.dokhorkhan')]'s influence on the steppes.\nYou never asked for this and the youngsters can be really annoying with their pestering but, if you are honest with yourself, you are intrigued to see if you can win this and have your name known for something other than petty cruelty and repeated political blunders.\nDokhor-Khan's forces are strong however and the Black Tortoise Court is eating on the palm of his hand. If you want to survive, let alone triumph, with the ragtag group of refugees under your command, you will have to think differently, pick your fights, raid and ambush when needed.\n\nGood thing fighting dirty has always been your strong suit."
